<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Rand will weaken til inflation tamed - S.African min.</title>
<headline>Rand will weaken til inflation tamed - S.African min.</headline>
<dateline>CAPE TOWN 1997-01-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>South African Finance Minister Trevor Manuel said in remarks broadcast on Sunday that the rand would continue to weaken until inflation was firmly under control.</p>
<p>Asked during a television talk show what direction he thought the currency would take in the new year, Manuel said:</p>
<p>&quot;I foresee an eight percent reduction a year... until we are really riding this tiger of inflation.&quot;</p>
<p>The rand has lost about 30 percent of its value since mid- February last year. South African inflation is running at around nine percent a year.</p>
<p>-- Cape Town newsroom +2721 252-238</p>
